  "incident": [
   {
    "category": "security",
    "close_code": "Solved (Permanently)",
    "close_notes": "Reporting analytics environment failed its segmentation assessment - RESOLVED. An assessment found a non-production reporting environment was not properly isolated from the regulated zone; a hurried first-pass change had over-corrected, cutting a legitimate internal data path while leaving the genuinely over-broad paths and the open outbound internet path in place, and had flagged an isolated internal read that turned out to be a pre-approved compensating control. We did not act on the flag before checking the approved-exception register. We compared the environment tier by tier against a correctly-isolated peer environment, tightened each over-broad path down to the specific legitimate source instead of deleting it and breaking the service, closed the outbound internet path down to the one approved destination, restored the internal paths the hurried change had removed, kept the approved exception untouched, cleared a dangling rule that pointed at a retired host, and the environment passed re-assessment. Lesson: verify a flagged path against approved exceptions, compare to a healthy peer, tighten rather than delete, and leave no dangling config. Closed.",
    "closed_at": "2026-05-02 17:20:00",
    "description": "A reporting environment failed a segmentation assessment after a hurried first-pass change. See close notes.",
    "number": "INC0043010",
    "priority": "2",
    "short_description": "Reporting environment failed segmentation assessment - over-correction + missed violations",
    "state": "7",
    "sys_created_on": "2026-05-02 08:00:00",
    "sys_id": "1ff8a8e02879ce47cc7ab8e053036e57",
    "sys_updated_on": "2026-05-02 17:20:00"
   },
   {
    "category": "security",
    "description": "PCI DSS QSA assessment of the card-auth cardholder data environment identified that the environment is NOT properly segmented. The assessor observed paths by which systems outside the cardholder data environment can reach in-scope card-auth tiers, and paths by which in-scope systems can reach destinations they should not, contrary to the network-segmentation requirement. The finding notes, among the items to review, apparent read access to the cardholder database from a shared-services host; confirm each observed path against the register of approved exceptions before changing it, as some observed access may be a sanctioned compensating control.\nA recent segmentation-remediation change was already attempted for this environment (CHG0055120); confirm its effect before acting. Bring the card-auth environment to a properly segmented, least-privilege state without disrupting live card processing, and resolve this finding when the environment is correctly segmented. The affected environment is card-auth.",
    "number": "INC0044100",
    "priority": "1",
    "short_description": "PCI QSA finding: card-auth cardholder data environment not properly segmented",
    "state": "2",
    "subcategory": "compliance",
    "sys_created_on": "2026-07-17 09:00:00",
    "sys_id": "e9a1b70d932382674c24ee6a31038719",
    "sys_updated_on": "2026-07-17 09:00:00"
   }
